    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L; amd §§4, 5, 7 & 16, Chap 272 of 1991; add §6-a, Chap of 2019 (as proposed in S.4940-B and A.7081)",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6304\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to revising\nthe period of authorization for the county of Westchester's additional\none percent rate of sales and compensating use tax and the expiration of\nthe Westchester county spending limitation act; to amend chapter 272 of\nthe laws of 1991, amending the tax law relating to the method of dispo-\nsition of sales and compensating use tax revenue in Westchester county\nand enacting the Westchester county spending limitation act, in relation\nto revising the period of authorization for the county of Westchester's\nadditional one percent rate of sales; and to amend a chapter of the laws\nof 2019, amending the tax law relating to authorizing the county of\nWestchester to impose an additional rate of sales and compensating use\ntax, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.4940-B and A.7081, in\nrelation to the period of authorization for Westchester's additional one\npercent rate of sales\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to ensure that Westchester County has a\nstable source of funding to continue providing community services.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Subparagraph (i) of the opening paragraph of section 1210 of\nthe tax law is amended by adding a new subdivision (42)\n\n§ 2. Amends Subdivision (a) of Section 1223 of the tax law is amended to\ninclude references to Westchester and ensure that that rate references\nare correct\n\n§ 3. Amends Subdivision (a) Section 1223 of the tax law is amended to\ninclude references to Westchester and ensure that that rate references\nare correct\n\n§ 4.Amends Section 1224 of the tax law is amended by adding a new para-\ngraph (ii)\n\n§ 5. Amends Section 1262-b of the tax law as adopted by chapter 272 of\nthe laws of 1991, as amended by section 1 of chapter 81 of the laws of\n2017, known as the \"Westchester County spending limitation act\"\n\n§ 6. Amends Subdivision e of section 4, and sections 5, 7 and 16 of\nchapter 272 of the laws of 1991, amending the tax law relating to the\nmethod of disposition of sales and compensating use tax revenue in West-\nchester County and enacting the Westchester county spending limitation\nact, as amended by chapter 81 of the laws of 2017.\n\n§ 7. Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWestchester has struggled to balance the budget as a result of not stay-\ning property tax cap compliant. As a result, the comptroller of New York\ndowngraded the credit of Westchester from AAA rating to AA1. Failure to\naddress the situation will ensure a structural deficit and exhaust the\nreserve budget by FY2021. Therefore, we must equalize rates among the\nrest of the County.\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2019, amending the tax law relating to authoriz-\ning the county of Westchester to impose an additional rate of 10 sales\nand compensating use tax, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n4940-B and A. 7081, takes effect.\n",
